{
  "rationale": "Evidence: iteration 7 (score 450.8) is the best design so far. Its oval finishes 19 of 20 runs at about 2.0 s, and the s-bend has progress 0.77 with 2 of 20 finishes. The slalom still fails at progress 0.16 with about 1.15 line-loss events per run. Max error sits at the 0.06 m off-track limit, and steering oscillation is moderate (0.2 to 0.4), so the robot is not jittering. It loses the line on fast direction changes. Iteration 6 showed that widening the 5-sensor array to ±0.06 m hurt the oval, so the array edge was not the fix in that form. Iteration 7 showed that raising kd from 0.9 to 1.2 helped on every track.\n\nChange: keep the controller from iteration 7 exactly, and change only the sensing geometry. Use 7 sensors at x = -0.045, -0.03, -0.015, 0, 0.015, 0.03, 0.045 (y = 0.06), with weights [-1.0, -0.667, -0.333, 0, 0.333, 0.667, 1.0]. This keeps the signal scale near ±1 so kp, kd and ki still mean the same thing. The array covers about the same span as before, but with finer spacing, so the signal changes more smoothly as the tape crosses the edge sensors. This tests H3 from iteration 7: that the slalom line loss comes from coarse edge resolution during fast direction changes. The 16 mm footprint is kept.\n\nExpected result: slalom line_loss_events should fall below 1.0 and its progress should rise above 0.16. Oval should hold near 0.95 finish rate and about 2 s. The overall score should rise above 451 if the finer array helps.\n\nHypotheses: (H1) the slalom failure is edge-resolution limited, so line loss drops with the finer array. (H2) if slalom still loses the line with similar line_loss_events, the limit is turn-in speed, and base_speed should drop to about 1.1 next. (H3) if the oval rms rises, the 7-sensor weighting is too coarse at centre and the centre weights should be reduced.\n\nMeasurements requested: all metrics per track, including completion, progress, completion_time, line_loss_events, max_error, rms_error and steering_oscillation, so that edge-loss effects can be separated from speed and overshoot.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.045, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.06},
      {"x": 0.045, "y": 0.06}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.18,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.2,
    "kp": 5.0,
    "ki": 4.0,
    "kd": 1.2,
    "sensor_weights": [-1.0, -0.667, -0.333, 0.0, 0.333, 0.667, 1.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "7-sensor finer array",
      "notes": "Keeps iteration 7's controller (best score 450.8) and changes only the sensing: 7 sensors at 15 mm spacing over ±0.045 m, to test whether coarse edge resolution causes the slalom line losses. Expect slalom line-loss events to fall and progress to rise."
    }
  }
}
